  <running_head>P. VOET</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>quòd</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">Unde lecti tyrones sub campi</l>
    <l n="2">doctore severè instruebantur</l>
    <l n="3">quo singuli periti forent, man-</l>
    <l n="4">data in prælio accipere, &amp; si</l>
    <l n="5">opus esset, etiam dare. Ut haut[?]</l>
    <l n="6">immerito de iisdem fuerit di-</l>
    <l n="7">ctum, quemvis militem ducis</l>
    <l n="8">partibus, &amp; quemvis ducem</l>
    <l n="9">militis officio fungi potuisse.</l>
    <l n="10">Quo nomine etiam nonnulli</l>
    <l n="11">inter Romanos laudatissimi,</l>
    <l n="12">quod nullum non armorum</l>
    <l n="13">exercitium in promptu habe-</l>
    <l n="14">rent. Pompejus certè Magni</l>
    <l n="15">titulo decoratus est, quod pro</l>
    <l n="16">consueto habuerit, saltu cum</l>
    <l n="17">alacribus, cursu cum velocibus,</l>
    <l n="18">vecte cum robustis certare. Et</l>
    <l n="19">de Aureliano Imperatore re-</l>
    <l n="20">fertur, eum nullum diem præ-</l>
    <l n="21">termisisse, in quo non se pilo,</l>
    <l n="22">sagittis, aliisq; militaribus ar-</l>
    <l n="23">mis exercerer. Quo etiam po-</l>
    <l n="24">tissimum nomine, dum de Sci-</l>
    <l n="25">pionis indole loquitur, Silius</l>
    <l n="26">Italicus, eundem commendat,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Catchword "quòd" at bottom right. "haut" is possibly printed for "haud"; left as printed and marked [?]. Ligature ct in "dictum" and "lecti" read as ct. Long s rendered as s throughout. A faint watermark ("Google") at bottom right is omitted.</notes>
